T PageQueue                    | RequestQueue.h | 45-80   | owning                        | -  | The drained demands of one rotation, in first-arrival order and coalesced. then spends itself against. Ordering by occurrence count instead would promote the largest surface before the one under the cursor, which is exactly backwards. demand with a count of a million, and the count is what a presenter reads to say how badly it is wanted — not what the ordering reads.
