T RequestQueue                 | RequestQueue.h | 94-125  | owning                        | -  | The demands sampling wrote, held per rotation slot until the readback latency has elapsed. cell must produce something immediately — the coarsest resident level — rather than stalling. A residency system that stalls on demand has converted a memory problem into a frame-time problem. With the two sharing a slot the drain would read demands recorded moments earlier and the latency would be zero on the tick and the full depth on every other, which is worse than either.
    has   SlotCount        static constexpr std::uint32_t  [-]  ?
    has   RotationSlots    PageQueue[SlotCount]            [-]  ?
    has   RecordedDemands  std::uint64_t                   [-]  ?
    by    Api/ImpressionSequence.h, Api/PreviewProjection.h, Api/SurfaceTileSpace.h, Source/ConsoleHost.cpp, Source/ImpressionSequence.cpp, Source/PreviewProjection.cpp, (+2 more)
    note  🔴 `20` §2.1 ②: demands are read back with a latency of the **rotation depth**. Sampling a non-resident
    note  📝 One slot more than the rotation depth, so the slot being written is never the slot being read.

